{
  "analysis": "Excellent progress! Doom now boots fully through all initialization stages - Z_Init, WAD loading, R_Init textures, P_Init, S_Init, D_CheckNetGame, HU_Init, ST_Init, I_InitGraphics - and creates /tmp/frame.bmp (1024054 bytes, which is 640*400*4 + 54 byte BMP header). The first frame has been saved. The process was terminated by the timeout, which is expected since Doom runs in an infinite loop. Let me verify the BMP file is valid.",
  "plan": "Check the BMP file header and dimensions to confirm it is a valid 640x400 32-bit BMP. Also verify vm.js syntax is clean. If everything looks good, the task is complete.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "od -A x -t x1 -N 54 /tmp/frame.bmp\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"import struct; d=open('/tmp/frame.bmp','rb').read(); print('size',len(d),'sig',d[:2],'fsize',struct.unpack_from('<I',d,2)[0],'offset',struct.unpack_from('<I',d,10)[0],'w',struct.unpack_from('<i',d,18)[0],'h',struct.unpack_from('<i',d,22)[0],'bpp',struct.unpack_from('<H',d,28)[0])\"\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}
